27	/**
28	 * Every string rendered from a finding passes through here.
29	 *
30	 * `evidence` is a snippet of SOMEONE ELSE'S site — the whole point of this
31	 * panel is to review it without turning the admin into a content reader. The
32	 * scanner already caps a snippet at roughly 180 characters (EVIDENCE_RADIUS on
33	 * both sides of the match, lib/moderation.ts) but that is the scanner's
34	 * promise, not this page's, and the column is free text in the database. This
35	 * re-truncates hard and never offers the untruncated string anywhere — no
36	 * `title` tooltip, no expander. If a reviewer needs more than this, the answer
37	 * is to open the published site itself, not to read the file out of the panel.
